Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Exa depends on open-source Dart and Flutter packages, listed with exact
versions in exa_mobile/pubspec.lock. Each is used under its own licence
(mostly BSD-3-Clause, MIT and Apache-2.0). Notable exceptions and notes:

- enough_mail - Mozilla Public License 2.0. Its source is available at
  https://github.com/Enough-Software/enough_mail
- pdfrx - MIT; bundles PDFium (BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0).
- Fonts (Fraunces, Plus Jakarta Sans) are fetched at runtime by google_fonts
  and are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

The licence text of every bundled package can be viewed inside the app.

On-device AI models are NOT included in this repository or in Exa builds.
They are downloaded by the user, and are subject to their own terms:

- Gemma 3 / Gemma 3n - Gemma Terms of Use, https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
- Qwen2.5 - Apache License 2.0

Remote AI providers (Anthropic, DeepSeek, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
are used under the user's own account and are subject to that provider's
terms.
